During photosynthesis $\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}$ is oxidised in photo system II with the release of $\mathrm{O}_2$, electron and proton at the oxygen - evolving complex.
Sodium hexa metaphosphate is used in calgon process for removing permanent hardness of water
$$
\mathrm{Na}_2\left[\mathrm{Na}_4\left(\mathrm{PO}_3\right)_6\right] \rightarrow \text{ calgon. }
$$
Hardness of $\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}$ is due to sulphates or chlorides of $\mathrm{Ca}$ and $\mathrm{Mg}$.
$$
\begin{aligned}
& \mathrm{Na}_2\left[\mathrm{Na}_4\left(\mathrm{PO}_3\right)_6\right]+\mathrm{Ca}^{2+} \rightarrow \mathrm{Na}_2\left[\mathrm{Ca}_2\left(\mathrm{PO}_3\right)_6\right]+\mathrm{Na}^{+} \\
& \mathrm{Na}_2\left[\mathrm{Na}_4\left(\mathrm{PO}_3\right)_6\right]+\mathrm{Mg}^{2+} \rightarrow \mathrm{Na}_2\left[\mathrm{Mg}_2\left(\mathrm{PO}_3\right)_6\right]+\mathrm{Na}^{+}
\end{aligned}
$$

